course: dictionary
lesson: 10371
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A treadmill is a machine with a moving belt. You walk or run on it, but you stay in the same place, because the belt moves the ground under your feet.
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so read the words around the word to find the right one. «I'm stuck on the treadmill» does not mean a gym machine. The clue is «stuck»: it means your days feel the same and tiring, with no way out.
explain: The word also has a history. The example sentence says that in Victorian prisons, prisoners walked for hours on a treadwheel, «a huge turning wheel of steps», and that is where the word treadmill comes from. The clue is «treadwheel»: it tells you the old treadmill was a wheel that people walked on.
fact: A treadmill is an exercise machine with a moving belt that you walk or run on without going anywhere.
fact: Treadmill can also mean a boring routine of work that goes on and on and never seems to get anywhere.
fact: Long ago, a treadmill was a large wheel turned by people or animals walking on it, used to grind grain or pump water.
fact: In Victorian prisons, a treadmill was used as a punishment, and prisoners walked on it for hours.
fact: Children should never use a treadmill without an adult, because fingers and clothes can get caught in the moving parts.
exercise: Lena walks fast on the treadmill at the gym, but she never leaves the spot. Where is Lena? | *On an exercise machine in a gym | In a shop buying shoes | On a train to the coast | At the top of a hill
exercise: «Every day is the same: school, homework, bed. I feel stuck on a treadmill.» What does treadmill mean here? | A bicycle with a basket | *A boring routine that never seems to get anywhere | A large wheel for grinding grain | A fast moving belt in a gym
exercise: What is the safety rule for treadmills? | *Only use one with an adult nearby | Always start at the fastest speed | Hold the moving belt to steady yourself | Jump on while the belt is already running
test: «Long ago, people walked on a huge turning wheel to grind grain.» What kind of treadmill is this? | A machine for printing books | *A wheel turned by walking | A kind of bread | A kind of boat
test: Which meaning of treadmill is figurative, not a real machine? | *A boring routine that never gets anywhere | A grain grinder in a mill | An exercise belt you run on | A wheel turned by animals
exam: The sentence says «a huge turning wheel of steps». What does this clue tell you about the old treadmill? | It was a lesson at school | *It was a turning wheel that people walked on | It was a flat belt in a gym | It was a ship that sailed the seas
